WEBVTT

00:00:16.141 --> 00:00:22.416
<v><b>Speaker:</b></v> In an acting career which covered 60 years in theatre, in film, and on TV,

00:00:22.798 --> 00:00:28.073
from Shakespeare, to Bond, to <i>Game of Thrones</i>, Diana Rigg was an icon,

00:00:28.271 --> 00:00:32.899
not only for her acting talent, but also for her incredible style.

00:00:34.060 --> 00:00:37.644
Diana was born in Doncaster, in the north of England,

00:00:37.867 --> 00:00:42.659
but she lived for the first eight years of her life in Jodhpur, in India,

00:00:42.897 --> 00:00:45.605
where her father, Louis, was a railway engineer.

00:00:47.644 --> 00:00:52.456
Diana returned to the UK with her mother, Beryl, in 1945.

00:00:55.181 --> 00:00:59.021
She went to boarding school, where she acted in many plays.

00:00:59.787 --> 00:01:04.127
Her teachers recognized her talent, and when she finished school,

00:01:04.425 --> 00:01:08.919
she studied drama at RADA, the Royal Academy of Dramatic Art.

00:01:11.218 --> 00:01:17.376
After RADA, in 1959, she got a job with the Royal Shakespeare Company.

00:01:17.907 --> 00:01:22.923
Diana made her debut in 1961, playing important roles

00:01:22.924 --> 00:01:28.117
such as Helena in <i>A Midsummer Night’s Dream</i>, and Cordelia in <i>King Lear</i>.

00:01:28.683 --> 00:01:34.072
She was part of a group of brilliant young actors, including Judi Dench.

00:01:38.289 --> 00:01:43.187
Diana didn’t earn much money in the theatre, so she also worked as a model,

00:01:43.430 --> 00:01:45.518
and had some small TV roles.

00:01:47.453 --> 00:01:53.510
However, in 1965, she got the role of secret agent Emma Peel

00:01:53.738 --> 00:01:58.001
in a very popular TV series called <i>The Avengers</i>.

00:01:58.765 --> 00:02:05.275
Overnight she became a star, but she continued to work with the Royal Shakespeare Company.

00:02:05.846 --> 00:02:08.239
She filmed <i>The Avengers</i> during the day,

00:02:08.581 --> 00:02:12.289
and then played Shakespearean roles in the theatre at night.

00:02:13.752 --> 00:02:18.249
At this time, women actors were usually paid less than men,

00:02:18.805 --> 00:02:22.733
but in her second season in <i>The Avengers</i>, she fought to

00:02:22.734 --> 00:02:26.630
get paid the same as the male star, Patrick Macnee.

00:02:28.954 --> 00:02:34.135
Her salary went up from £150 a week to £450,

00:02:34.616 --> 00:02:39.346
though she said later that no other women in the profession supported her.

00:02:41.811 --> 00:02:46.620
After leaving <i>The Avengers</i>, she had many roles in successful films.

00:02:47.161 --> 00:02:52.935
In 1969, she was a Bond girl in the film <i>On Her Majesty’s Secret Service</i>,

00:02:53.371 --> 00:02:56.722
and played the only woman James Bond ever married.

00:02:59.500 --> 00:03:04.783
Diana won many awards for her acting, both in the US and in the UK,

00:03:05.274 --> 00:03:09.895
including an Emmy for her role in <i>Rebecca</i> (in 1997).

00:03:12.233 --> 00:03:19.487
In 1994, she was made a Dame Commander of the Order of the British Empire, or DBE.

00:03:21.090 --> 00:03:26.127
For many of the younger generation, who did not know her in her early roles,

00:03:26.459 --> 00:03:33.348
Diana became a star again in the hit HBO series <i>Game of Thrones</i> when,

00:03:33.349 --> 00:03:40.732
from 2013 to 2017, she played Lady Olenna Tyrell, ‘Queen of Thorns’.

00:03:43.247 --> 00:03:47.307
Her last role was in 2021, in the horror film

00:03:47.411 --> 00:03:51.335
<i>Last Night in Soho</i>, where she played the main villain.

00:03:52.049 --> 00:03:56.812
The film was still in production when she died in September 2020,

00:03:57.055 --> 00:04:00.877
aged 82, and it is dedicated to her.

00:04:02.568 --> 00:04:06.355
Diana Rigg married twice, and had a daughter, Rachael,

00:04:06.420 --> 00:04:10.470
with her second husband, Archie Stirling, a theatre producer.

00:04:11.470 --> 00:04:16.041
When she discovered that Stirling was having an affair, Diana divorced him

00:04:16.270 --> 00:04:19.473
and took all his suits to the nearest charity shop!

00:04:20.493 --> 00:04:24.516
Diana Rigg loved life, and lived it to the full.

00:04:25.097 --> 00:04:31.012
On her 80th birthday, she had an enormous party where she invented a cocktail

00:04:31.154 --> 00:04:35.648
called Dame Diana’s Dynamite, and danced all night.

00:04:36.461 --> 00:04:40.480
One of the last things she said to her daughter before she died was,

00:04:41.047 --> 00:04:43.981
‘Oh, but I’ve had such a life!’